# UI Permission Gating = Server Permission

When showing or hiding action-menu items, buttons, or nav affordances, use the **same permission string** the mutation/query checks on the server (`requireOrgPermission` / `requireClassPermission`). Do not invent coarser UI-only flags.

Server authz remains the real boundary; UI gating is UX only.

## Lookups (keep O(1))

| Context | Helper | Notes |
|---------|--------|-------|
| Home org/class lists | `roleHasPermission(role, "…")` from `@rbac-catalog` | Role must already be on the list item (e.g. `org.role`, `classDoc.role` from `listMine`). No per-card permission queries. |
| Inside an org | `hasOrgPermission(permissions, "…")` via `useCurrentOrgPermissions` | One live permissions query per page; `Set.has` is O(1). |
| Inside a class | `hasClassPermission(permissions, "…")` via `useCurrentClassPermissions` | Same pattern. |

## Per-item, not whole-menu

If actions map to different permissions, gate each item separately. Hide the ⋮ trigger when no items remain.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — update unlocks delete in the UI
const canManage = roleHasPermission(org.role, "organizations:update");
// menu always shows Edit + Delete

// ✅ GOOD — match tenants.updateOrganization vs tenants.deleteOrganization
const canUpdate = roleHasPermission(org.role, "organizations:update");
const canDelete = roleHasPermission(org.role, "organizations:delete");
```

Extra server constraints beyond a permission string (e.g. class delete also requires owner) must be mirrored in the UI.

